## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/solvepoissonmultigrid.html
- Summary (EN): Solve Poisson Multigrid solves Poisson's equation over a rectangular layer using a geometric multigrid V-cycle. It is commonly used for pressure projection in fluid simulations, including inside the Flow Project Non-Divergent Multigrid and Flow Block nodes.
- Résumé (FR) : Solve Poisson Multigrid résout l'équation de Poisson sur un calque rectangulaire par un cycle V multigrille, typiquement pour la projection de pression en simulation de fluide.

- Inputs meaning: ["rhs: mono layer containing the residual"]

- Key parameters: ["Output: mono layer named solution", "Iterations: number of V-cycles, more improves accuracy and costs time", "Smoothing Method: Gauss-Seidel (in place, less memory, converges better) or Jacobi (avoids checkerboard residuals, needs an extra copy)", "Up / Down Smoothing Iterations: smoothing passes after prolongation and before restriction", "Coarsest Smoothing Iterations: smoothing passes at the coarsest level, used in place of an exact solve", "Target Coarse Dimensions: sets when coarsening stops, larger gives fewer levels and more unknowns at the coarsest level", "X Borders / Y Borders: Open = Dirichlet (value 0), Closed = Neumann (zero normal derivative), Periodic = wrapped edges"]

- Caveats: ["Coarsest Smoothing Iterations should be on the order of the square of Target Coarse Dimensions", "Raising Target Coarse Dimensions generally requires more coarsest-level iterations", "Higher iteration counts trade speed for accuracy", "Separate from Solve Poisson, which solves inside a 2D signed distance boundary"]

